mutated_response:
You can declare the HTTP status code for a response in decorators like `@app.get()` by using the `status_code` parameter. This parameter receives a number with the HTTP status code or an `IntEnum`, such as Python's `http.HTTPStatus`. 

Here is how you can do it:

```python
@app.get(status_code=200)
@app.post(status_code=201)
@app.put(status_code=200)
@app.delete(status_code=204)
```

or 

```python
from http import HTTPStatus

@app.get(status_code=HTTPStatus.OK)
@app.post(status_code=HTTPStatus.CREATED)
@app.put(status_code=HTTPStatus.OK)
@app.delete(status_code=HTTPStatus.NO_CONTENT)
```

